n of about R+8. Jace Yarbrough won the crowded Republican primary without a runoff after his main rival dropped out, backed by a Trump endorsement and outside spending exceeding $1.5 million. Democrat Dan Barrios has raised under $100,000 and has minimal cash on hand.\n\nNo general-election polling is available, so the outlook rests on fundamentals, expert ratings, and markets. Raters across the spectrum call the seat Likely or Solid Republican, and prediction markets put Democratic odds near 10%. Yarbrough's polarizing profile is the main source of uncertainty in an otherwise Republican-favored race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.087, "margin": -8.61}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.08, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0959, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0932, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0678, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0506, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0649, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1129, "margin": -8.5}]}